      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Typical bee-eaters — brilliantly coloured, slender birds specialised for catching bees, wasps, and other flying insects on the wing. They remove the sting by rubbing the prey against a perch before swallowing. Their dazzling plumage — combinations of green, blue, yellow, and chestnut — make them among the most beautiful of all birds. Most species are migratory, wintering in Africa.",
